spec.md

# --- internal docs & reports -------------------------------------------------
# Repo root IS the deploy root here (outputDirectory ".", cleanUrls true), so
# every tracked file is a live URL. On 2026-07-25 an audit found 18 internal
# files served 200 and crawlable on this domain, including CLAUDE.md,
# OWNER_ACTIONS_GITDEALFLOW.md and the HERMES conversion reports — i.e. the
# unpublished go-to-market plan for the one site in the portfolio with paying
# customers. Globs, not exact names, so the families this repo keeps generating
# are caught as they appear.
CLAUDE.md
HERMES_*.md
REPORT_*.md
OWNER_*.md
*AUDIT*.md
*SCORECARD*.md

# Editor / conversion leftovers. Untracked today (inline.css.bak-conv,
# ux.css.bak-conv, ux.css.bak2 are all sitting in this directory right now), so
# one `git add` away from being served — and a stale copy of the live stylesheet
# is exactly the kind of file that gets indexed and then contradicts the real one.
*.bak
*.bak-conv
*.bak*

# --- internal tooling: pSEO / i18n generators and ops scripts ---------------
# These were served publicly too. No credentials were found in them — the
# IndexNow key in scripts/indexnow-ping.mjs is public by design, served at
# /<key>.txt as the verification mechanism — so this was information disclosure
# rather than credential exposure.
_*.py
_*.mjs
data/momentum-index/_build_momentum_index.mjs

# scripts/ CANNOT be excluded wholesale here, unlike churnlens and carshake.
# vercel.json's buildCommand IS `node scripts/verify-jsonld.mjs .`, so Vercel
# needs that file present in the build container; a bare `scripts/` entry was
# committed in 729779f1 and would have failed EVERY deploy of this domain with
# "Cannot find module" — on the one site in the portfolio with paying customers,
# which growth-loop auto-deploys with an un-gated `vercel deploy --prod`.
#
# So exclude the directory's *contents* and re-include only the gate. This is the
# one place this file uses `!` negation, and it is load-bearing in both
# directions: `scripts/*` (not `scripts/`) is required, because gitignore
# semantics cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded.
# Verify changes to this file empirically, do not read them and assume. Copy it to
# .gitignore in an empty `git init` directory, recreate the paths, and run
# `git check-ignore` there — git implements the same rules Vercel does. It must be
# an empty directory, not this repo: slash-anchored patterns like `scripts/*`
# resolve against the ignore file's own root, which is landing/ for Vercel but
# signals-gitdealflow/ for a checkout, so testing in place silently reports the
# wrong answer for exactly the rule that can break every deploy.
#
# Consequence to accept knowingly: /scripts/verify-jsonld.mjs stays a public URL.
# 37c6ea8a already weighed that and it still holds — it is a generic linter with
# no secrets, no keys and no site-specific data.
scripts/*
!scripts/verify-jsonld.mjs
!scripts/verify-vercel-config.mjs
!scripts/verify-momentum-widget.mjs
!scripts/verify-word-floor.mjs
!scripts/verify-direct-answers.mjs
!scripts/verify-no-dashes.mjs
!scripts/verify-css-preloads.mjs
!scripts/verify-pricing-offers.mjs
!scripts/verify-all.mjs
!scripts/verify-author-identity.mjs
!scripts/verify-crawl-proxy.mjs
!scripts/verify-claims.mjs
!scripts/indexnow-ping.mjs

# NEVER add a bare `scripts/` line. It reads like the right hardening, churnlens
# and carshake both have one, and here it fails every deploy — see above.
#
# DO NOT add these to .vercelignore — they are served on purpose as static files:
#   agents.md                                       -> AI/AEO discovery surface (markdown)
#   <hex>.txt                                       -> IndexNow key verification
#   google*.html, BingSiteAuth.xml                  -> search-engine verification
#   mcp-demo.gif                                    -> see CLAUDE.md, do not remove
#   data/startup-ma-statistics/data.csv             -> CC BY datasets, each cited
#   research/vc-deal-flow-signal-2026/data.csv         from its own landing page
#
# NOTE: the AI discovery files are now llms.src.txt, llms-full.src.txt, ai.src.txt,
# agents.src.txt. Their PUBLIC paths (/llms.txt etc.) are served by api/crawl-proxy.js
# (which logs bot_crawl to PostHog), so the .src source files have no public /llms.txt
# static twin and the rewrite can fire. The .src files themselves stay static (harmless).

# --- agent working files ---
# Preventive. carshake shipped 1,171 files this way on 2026-07-26 — a full
# Claude Code worktree under .claude/, live and indexable on the production
# domain, because the repo root is the deploy root there too. Nothing to
# exclude here today; this is the guard for the day an agent session creates
# one. It is untracked, so `git status` would never show it.
/.claude
